@*
    The branded 404 visual, shared by two entry points:
      * Routes.razor <NotFound> — signed-in users hitting an unknown path
        (the Blazor catch-all endpoint matches, the Router doesn't).
      * /not-found page — UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute re-runs body-less
        404s from non-Blazor endpoints against it.
*@

<PageTitle>Page not found — DueMap</PageTitle>

<div class="min-h-[60vh] flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-16">
    <div class="text-center max-w-md">
        <div class="inline-flex w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-primary-soft items-center justify-center text-primary mb-5">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="m16.24 7.76-2.12 6.36-6.36 2.12 2.12-6.36z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading tabular-nums">404</div>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-heading">That page doesn't exist</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            The link may be out of date, or the address was mistyped.
            Nothing has been lost — your data is right where you left it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
            <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Go to dashboard</a>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="history.back()">Go back</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
